schema: source-system
object:
  title: SuperBenefit Knowledge Garden
  type: knowledge-garden
  url: https://knowledge.superbenefit.org/
  steward: SuperBenefit (a DAO researching web3 systems-change)
  what_it_curates: >-
    A public knowledge garden organized into four section types — Docs
    (finished explanations/guides), Lexicon (shared-vocabulary definitions),
    Links (annotated external resources), and Patterns (reusable solutions
    to recurring governance/coordination problems) — including a published
    "Knowledge Gardens" pattern describing SuperBenefit's own gardening
    practice (gardeners, sensemaking sessions, seasonal reviews).
  why_it_matters: >-
    A live, real-world worked example of the garden model this toolkit
    article recommends: a durable community knowledge structure that
    outlives contributor turnover, cited as the model to copy.
  how_to_credit: Credit SuperBenefit and link to https://knowledge.superbenefit.org/
  return_path: >-
    Not specified in source article beyond the public garden URL — engage
    via SuperBenefit's public knowledge garden site; no explicit
    contribute-back/PR process was documented in this source, flagged for
    follow-up (see notes).
  currentness: >-
    Article notes SuperBenefit ran Obsidian+Quartz before migrating to a
    custom Astro build; currentness of the garden's tooling as of the
    article's writing (2026), not independently re-verified here.
  extraction_status: raw AI-assisted extraction from a single toolkit article — not independently verified against the live site
  toolkit_route: Layer 2 (Knowledge Commons) / Layer 4 (Concept Lineage) — pattern-library peer
  maturity: raw
  public_use: source-linked-unreviewed
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/knowledge-gardens.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  notes: >-
    return_path is a best-effort inference (the article only links to the
    garden's homepage) — a human reviewer should confirm SuperBenefit's
    actual contribute-back mechanism (Discord, GitHub, contact form) before
    promoting this card past raw.
